==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Ritual Drum Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Festive Otter]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**8 [[Festive Otter]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**1 [[Festive Otter]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Start stacking up [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cats]], then spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] once you have enough cash. There is absolutely no concern to be had about money, as the onslaught of enemies will provide you with more than enough. Instead, you should worry about defending as well as you can against them: 3 or more meatshields + Area/Piercing Attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]/[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] will be especially useful. As long as you keep stacking up long-ranged attackers, you should eventually outlast the Festival Otters.

==Trivia ==
*Backyard BBQ's Japanese name, Kimi ga Ita Natsumatsuri ("The Summer Festival You Were In"), is a reference to the lyric "Kimi ga ita natsu wa tōi yume no naka" ("The memory of a summer with you is in a distant dream") from the song "[https://youtu.be/BFvdvIFsvPg Natsumatsuri]" ("Summer Festival") by [[wikipedia:ja:JITTERIN'JINN|JITTERIN'JINN]].

